verified":true},{"surface":"மகளிர்","parts":[{"text":"மகளிர்","lemma":"makaḷir","gloss":"women"}],"gloss":"women"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அல்குல்","parts":[{"text":"அல்குல்","lemma":"alkul","gloss":"hips/loins"}],"gloss":"hips"},{"surface":"தாங்கா","parts":[{"text":"தாங்கா","lemma":"tāṅkā","gloss":"not bearing"}],"gloss":"not bearing"},{"surface":"அசைஇ","parts":[{"text":"அசைஇ","lemma":"acaii","gloss":"moving/swaying"}],"gloss":"swaying"},{"surface":"மெல்லென","parts":[{"text":"மெல்","lemma":"mel","gloss":"gentle"},{"text":"என","lemma":"eṉa","gloss":"as"}],"gloss":"gently"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"கலங்கலந்","parts":[{"text":"கலங்கலந்","lemma":"கலங்கலந்","gloss":"unclarified"}],"gloss":"unclarified","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"தேறல்","parts":[{"text":"தேறல்","lemma":"tēṟal","gloss":"clear liquor"}],"gloss":"liquor"},{"surface":"பொலங்கலத்து","parts":[{"text":"பொலங்கலத்து","lemma":"பொலங்கலத்து","gloss":"in golden vessels"}],"gloss":"in golden vessels","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"ஏந்தி","parts":[{"text":"ஏந்தி","lemma":"ēnti","gloss":"holding"}],"gloss":"holding"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அமிழ்தென","parts":[{"text":"அமிழ்து","lemma":"amiḻtu","gloss":"nectar"},{"text":"என","lemma":"eṉa","gloss":"like"}],"gloss":"like nectar"},{"surface":"மடுப்ப","parts":[{"text":"மடுப்ப","lemma":"maṭuppa","gloss":"to serve/feed"}],"gloss":"serving"},{"surface":"மாந்தி","parts":[{"text":"மாந்தி","lemma":"mānti","gloss":"drinking"}],"gloss":"drinking"},{"surface":"இகழ்விலன்","parts":[{"text":"இகழ்வு","lemma":"ikaḻvu","gloss":"negligence/disregard"},{"text":"இலன்","lemma":"ilaṉ","gloss":"he is without"}],"gloss":"without negligence"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"நில்லா","parts":[{"text":"நில்லா","lemma":"nillā","gloss":"unstable/transient"}],"gloss":"unstable"},{"surface":"உலகத்து","parts":[{"text":"உலகத்து","lemma":"உலகத்து","gloss":"of the world"}],"gloss":"of the world","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"நிலையாமைநீ","parts":[{"text":"நிலையாமை","lemma":"nilaiyāmai","gloss":"impermanence"},{"text":"நீ","lemma":"nī","gloss":"you"}],"gloss":"impermanence, you"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"சொல்லா","parts":[{"text":"சொல்லா","lemma":"சொல்லா","gloss":"to say"}],"gloss":"to say","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"வேண்டா","parts":[{"text":"வேண்டா","lemma":"vēṇṭā","gloss":"not needed"}],"gloss":"is not needed"},{"surface":"தோன்றல்","parts":[{"text":"தோன்றல்","lemma":"tōṉṟal","gloss":"lord/leader"}],"gloss":"the lord"},{"surface":"முந்துஅறிந்த","parts":[{"text":"முந்து","lemma":"muntu","gloss":"beforehand"},{"text":"அறிந்த","lemma":"ariṉta","gloss":"known"}],"gloss":"known beforehand"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"முழுதுஉணர்","parts":[{"text":"முழுது","lemma":"muḻutu","gloss":"completely"},{"text":"உணர்","lemma":"uṇar","gloss":"understanding"}],"gloss":"completely understanding"},{"surface":"கேள்வியன்","parts":[{"text":"கேள்வி","lemma":"kēḷvi","gloss":"learning"},{"text":"அன்","lemma":"aṉ","gloss":"he who has"}],"gloss":"one of learning"},{"surface":"ஆகலின்","parts":[{"text":"ஆகலின்","lemma":"ākaliṉ","gloss":"since he is"}],"gloss":"since he is"},{"surface":"விரகினானே","parts":[{"text":"விரகினான்","lemma":"virakiṉāṉ","gloss":"one with wisdom/skill"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"indeed (emphasis)"}],"gloss":"with wisdom indeed"}]}],"literal":"The singer, the sung-about, the theme, and the sub-theme are not known. / Roaring like thunder facing the dark rainy season, with a loud clatter, / unsatisfied Death who causes distress to precious lives, / he does not fear your coming! Indeed, many good / sacrificial Brahmins who have completed their learning, / scattering rare ornaments with water, with great generosity / better than a mother, giving to many, / with great male elephants of disciplined gait, his / grace bestowing well on those who sing, / killing enemies with rolling-wheeled many chariots, and his / sweetly giving to those who seek refuge at his feet, / to the songstress wearing twisted garlands, / with the flower-like bards wearing golden lotuses, / with long dark hands that embraced them together, / with deer-like gaze, of chastity filled with patience, / with eyebrows curved like a bow, quickly / women with thorn-like teeth, whose speech fears if they grant love, / swaying gently, their hips unable to bear the weight, / holding unclarified liquor in golden vessels, / drinking it as if it were nectar served, without negligence, / the impermanence of this unstable world, you / need not speak of! The lord has known it beforehand, / since he is one of complete understanding and learning, with wisdom indeed.","translation":"The poet, the patron, the theme, and the sub-theme of this poem are lost to time. O Death, who roars like thunder in the dark rainy season with a loud clatter, and who is never satisfied as you cause distress to precious lives! Our lord does not fear your coming. To the Brahmins of sacrifices who have perfected their learning of the Vedas, he has poured out water and scattered rare ornaments, giving to many with a generosity greater than a mother's. He has bestowed great male elephants of disciplined gait on those who sing of his grace. He has destroyed his enemies with his rolling chariots, and sweetly given refuge to those who seek his feet. With his long, dark hands, he has embraced and welcomed the songstress wearing twisted garlands and the bards wearing golden lotuses. He has enjoyed the company of women with deer-like gazes, patient chastity, bow-curved eyebrows, and sharp, thorn-like teeth—women whose very speech makes one tremble when they grant their love, and who sway gently as they walk, their hips barely bearing their weight. He has drank the clear, unclarified liquor they served in golden vessels as if it were nectar, never losing his composure. Therefore, O Death, you do not need to lecture him on the impermanence of this unstable world! Our lord has known it long beforehand, for he is a man of complete understanding, deep learning, and profound wisdom.","modern":"இப்பாடலின் ஆசிரியர், பாடப்பட்ட தலைவன், திணை, துறை ஆகியவை அறியப்படவில்லை. கார்மேகத்து இடி முழக்கத்தைப் போல உரக்க ஒலித்து, அரிய உயிர்களைக் கவர்ந்து செல்லும், என்றும் பசியடங்காத கூற்றுவனே! எங்கள் தலைவன் உனது வருகைக்கு அஞ்சுபவன் அல்லன். அவன், வேதக் கேள்விகளில் முதிர்ந்த அந்தணர்களுக்கு அரிய அணிகலன்களை நீரோடு வாரியிறைத்து, தாயைக் காட்டிலும் மேலாகப் பலருக்கும் கொடையளித்தான். தன் புகழைப் பாடும் பாணர்களுக்கு ஒழுங்கான நடையையுடைய பெரிய ஆண் யானைகளைப் பரிசாக அளித்தான். உருளும் சக்கரங்களையுடைய தேர்களைக் கொண்டு பகைவர்களை அழித்து, தன் திருவடிகளை அடைந்தவர்களுக்கு இனிய கொடைகளை வழங்கினான். முறுக்கிய மாலைகளை அணிந்த பாடினிக்கும், பொன்னாலான தாமரை மலர்களை அணிந்த பாணர்களுக்கும் தன் நீண்ட கைகளால் அணைத்து ஆதரவு தந்தான். பொறுமையும் கற்பும் கொண்ட, மான் போன்ற பார்வையையும், வில் போன்ற புருவங்களையும், கூர்மையான பற்களையும் உடைய மகளிர், மெல்ல அசைந்து நடந்து, பொற்கலங்களில் ஏந்தித் தந்த தெளிந்த கள்ளினை அமிழ்தம் எனப் பருகி மகிழ்ந்தான். ஆகவே, நிலையற்ற இவ்வுலகத்தின் நிலையாமையைப் பற்றி நீ அவனுக்குச் சொல்ல வேண்டியதில்லை. அவன் எல்லாவற்றையும் உணர்ந்த பேரறிஞன் ஆதலால், இதனை ஏற்கனவே நன்கு அறிந்தவன் ஆவான்.","explanation":"This poem belongs to the Puṟam genre, though its specific poet, patron, and context are lost. The speaker addresses Yama, the God of Death, telling him that the great king or chieftain does not fear his arrival. The poem lists the king's noble deeds: his immense generosity to Vedic scholars, his patronage of bards and songstresses, his bravery in defeating enemies, and his refined enjoyment of life's pleasures with beautiful women. Because the king has lived a complete, virtuous, and generous life, enjoying both duty and pleasure, he is fully aware of the world's transience. Therefore, Death has no power to frighten him or teach him about impermanence, as the king's wisdom and legacy already transcend mortality. Key words like 'kūṟṟam' (death), 'īttu' (giving), and 'nilaiyāmai' (impermanence) highlight the poem's philosophical depth.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.7],[0.7,1.4],[1